RAWRXD_OVERLAY_FAMILY_SEARCH_001
==================================
THE LAST OPEN IDEA, TESTED AS AN OPTIMISATION RATHER THAN A GUESS.

TOOL   rawrxd/certs/gguf_tensor_slice_001.cpp  (stage 5)
QUESTION
    Stages 1-4 tested SPECIFIC bases -- the shipped formats. That answers
    "did this base work?", not "is there ANY base that works?"

    The proposal restated as an optimisation is:
        minimise   base_bpw + H(W - base)      over all bases
    Every point on the overlay's curve has rel_L2 = 0 BY CONSTRUCTION, because
    the delta is defined as W - base. So the whole overlay family collapses to
    ONE number: the minimum of that sum.

    If the MINIMUM loses to the direct curve, no base in the family rescues the
    architecture. That is far stronger than four failed formats.

FAMILY SEARCHED = RTN min/max over bits {1,2,3,4,5,6,8} x group {16,32,64,128,256}
ALL CASES PASS, CHECKS_FAIL=0


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. RESULT
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
tensor                    family_MIN_total   at (base_bpw, delta_H)   direct@0.05  margin
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MoE blk.20.ffn_down_exps        6.6186        1.5000 + 5.1186  (1b/32)     6.0000    +0.62
MoE blk.0.ffn_gate_exps         5.1992        2.0000 + 3.1992  (1b/16)     5.0000    +0.20
dense blk.31.attn_q             6.1296        4.5000 + 1.6296  (4b/32)     4.5000    +1.63
dense blk.63.ffn_down           8.4333        2.0000 + 6.4333  (1b/16)     5.2500    +3.18

  ANY_BASE_IN_FAMILY_BEATS_DIRECT = 0   in ALL FOUR cases


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. THE NUANCE THAT MATTERS MOST: THE OPTIMISATION WORKS, AND IS STILL NOT ENOUGH
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compare the family minimum against what the SHIPPED base achieved in stage 4:

  tensor                  shipped base total   optimised minimum   improvement
  MoE IQ3_XXS                    7.2993             6.6186           -9.3%
  MoE IQ2_XS                     7.2568             5.1992          -28.3%
  dense Q4_K                    11.7107             6.1296          -47.7%
  dense Q6_K                    13.4188             8.4333          -37.2%

So the proposed optimisation -- choose the base to minimise base_bpw plus
RESIDUAL entropy rather than base_bpw alone -- IS REAL AND IS SUBSTANTIAL. It
cuts the overlay's cost by 9-48%, and on dense Q4_K it nearly halves it.

It still loses. The architecture is not rescued, but the reason it loses is now
precise: not that the base was chosen badly, but that base_bpw + H(residual) has
a floor above the direct-quantiser cost for these tensors.

Note where the optimum lands. Three of the four choose a ONE-BIT base, pushing
almost everything into the delta. That is the optimiser correctly observing
that the base is nearly worthless as storage and the delta is doing the work --
which is a description of the overlay's failure mode, found by minimising it.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. THE CLOSEST CALL, STATED PLAINLY
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MoE blk.0.ffn_gate_exps (IQ2_XS): family minimum 5.1992 against a direct cost
of 5.0000 for rel_L2 <= 0.05. That is a 4.0% gap.

Every other case is 12-60% behind. This one is close enough that it should not
be rounded away, and it is the case where a base OUTSIDE the searched family
might plausibly win. It is a reason to keep the question open on one tensor,
not a reason to call the architecture viable.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT CLOSE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLOSES:
    Any base in {RTN min/max} x {bits 1..8} x {group 16..256}. The minimum over
    that family loses in 4/4. The low-rank framing is dead by the rank bound;
    the general overlay is dead by this minimisation.

DOES NOT CLOSE:
    Bases outside the family. In particular a base constructed so its error IS
    structured -- a learned codebook, a vector-quantised base, or a
    low-rank-plus-quantised base -- is not in this search, because RTN has no
    objective that would produce one. The measured optima landing on 1-bit
    bases are evidence that RTN actively WORKS AGAINST residual structure: a
    minimiser of base bits has no reason to shape the error.

    So the correct statement is: the overlay fails for every base that treats
    the base and the residual independently. It has NOT been tested against a
    base designed jointly with its residual -- which is a real gap, and the only
    one left.

FAMILY_SEARCH_IS_NOT_ALL_QUANTISERS = 1, reported by the tool itself.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. FINAL STATE OF THE PROPOSAL
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  LOW_RANK_RESIDUAL_VARIANT   REFUTED PROVABLY
      rank(W) <= rank(base) + rank(delta) puts the floor for any two-factor
      split at 36.9-38.6 bits/element for a 32-bit original.

  RESIDUAL_OVERLAY_GENERAL     REFUTED for every independently-chosen base
      family minimum 5.20-8.43 bpw against a direct 4.50-6.00 bpw for
      rel_L2 <= 0.05. Dominated 4/4, including after the base is optimised
      rather than assumed.

  DELTA_STRUCTURE              NONE FOUND
      not sparse, not low-rank, not low-entropy.

  THE ONE UNTESTED VARIANT
      A base optimised JOINTLY with its residual -- chosen so the error is
      sparse or low-rank by construction, rather than being whatever RTN's
      min/max happens to leave. The harness now measures both terms and the
      exact rank curve, so it is runnable without new instrumentation.

      The bar it must clear is a 0.20 bpw deficit on one MoE tensor and
      0.62-3.18 on the others, against a direct-format path that has not been
      beaten. That is a low bar on one case and a high one on the rest.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. LIMITS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Family is RTN only, by the tool's own report.
  * rel_L2 against one fixed Gaussian probe per tensor.
  * Windows 256x1024; four tensors; one MoE family and one dense model.
  * Residual entropy is order-0. Higher-order coding would lower the delta term
    and could move the margins -- this is stated because order-0 has been within
    a factor of ~1.1 of the 8-bit symbol everywhere measured, so the headroom is
    small but it is not zero.
  * No engine, GPU, I/O or residency linkage.

